 "stimulus_html": "<p>“I don't accept the idea that this is just a military action, that this is just a military effort, and every time we have had difficulties in South Vietnam and Southeast Asia we have had only one response, we have had only one way to deal with it - month after month - year after year we have dealt with it in only one way and that's to send more military men and increase our military power and I don't think that's what the kind of a struggle that it is in Southeast Asia. . . .</p>\n<p>. . . We can continue to escalate, we can continue to send more men there, until we have millions and millions of more men and we can continue to bomb North Vietnam, and in my judgment we will be no nearer success, we will be no nearer victory than we are now in February of 1968.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Robert F. Kennedy, Remarks at the University of Kansas, March 18, 1968</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>\n",
